homelab-prometheus (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: makes a host the fleet's Prometheus monitoring
    server. Depends on the Ubuntu-archive prometheus (2.53.x); a
    prometheus.service drop-in points it at /etc/prometheus/homelab/
    prometheus.yml (30d retention, :9090) whose scrape targets are
    file_sd files under targets/. homelab-prometheus-pull regenerates
    those from homelab-api's feature-backends view on a 2-min timer
    (pull model, reusing the local homelab-agent's system_agent
    credential), so scrape targets track the live fleet with no
    hand-edited lists. Ships services/prometheus.yml (topology
    visibility, kind: metrics-store) and an nftables egress drop-in
    opening only homelab-api + the fleet exporter ports from this host
    (applied live without flushing the ruleset, bad-ips-safe). Phase 1
    scrapes node_exporter (:9100) fleet-wide; further tiers are additive
    (a pull.yml jobs: entry + a scrape job).

 -- Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>  Tue, 30 Sep 2026 14:00:00 -0500
